Add resetCollectedInformation() to SystemInformationToolbarItem.

SystemInformationToolbarItem is an #[Autoconfigure(public: true)]
shared service whose collectInformation() appends to
$systemInformation[] on every call. After N requests every entry
appears N times in the toolbar dropdown.

Add a public resetCollectedInformation() method that clears all
accumulated state back to post-construction defaults.

--- a/Classes/Backend/ToolbarItems/SystemInformationToolbarItem.php
+++ b/Classes/Backend/ToolbarItems/SystemInformationToolbarItem.php
@@ -52,7 +52,23 @@
         private readonly Typo3Version $typo3Version,
         private readonly BackendViewFactory $backendViewFactory,
     ) {
+        $this->highestSeverity = InformationStatus::INFO;
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Resets all collected system information and messages to
+     * post-construction defaults.
+     *
+     * Useful for long-running PHP runtimes where this shared service
+     * persists across requests and collected information accumulates.
+     */
+    public function resetCollectedInformation(): void
+    {
+        $this->systemInformation = [];
+        $this->systemMessages = [];
+        $this->systemMessageTotalCount = 0;
         $this->highestSeverity = InformationStatus::INFO;
+        $this->severityBadgeClass = '';
     }
 
     public function setRequest(ServerRequestInterface $request): void
